{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"116408","commit":"65ce51272c570b65f6bac36474c978537f9e210e","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `instanceof AbstractQueryBuilder` check silently skips any `QueryBuilder` that does not extend `AbstractQueryBuilder`, meaning inner hits defined on such a builder would be dropped without any warning. While in practice most query builders extend `AbstractQueryBuilder`, a silent no-op here could mask a real bug. Consider adding a debug/log statement for the skipped case, or asserting that all entries are `AbstractQueryBuilder` instances during development.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/rankdoc/RankDocsQueryBuilder.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/RankDocsQueryBuilder.java--2214:2606","promptId":"#E39XP","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/rankdoc/RankDocsQueryBuilder.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/RankDocsQueryBuilder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2214,"endPos":2606,"startLine":56,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":65,"endLineOffset":5,"length":393}]}]},{"comment":"The `skipInnerHits` field is added to `SearchSourceBuilder` with a getter and setter, but it is not included in `SearchSourceBuilder`\u0027s own serialization protocol (it is serialized separately by `ShardSearchRequest`). This means that after deserialization on a data node, `source.skipInnerHits()` will always return `false`, while `request.skipInnerHits()` correctly returns the transmitted value. Any code path that reads `source.skipInnerHits()` post-deserialization will silently get the wrong answer. Consider either (a) documenting the field as transient/internal-only, or (b) removing the field from `SearchSourceBuilder` entirely and passing the flag as a separate constructor parameter to `ShardSearchRequest`, to avoid the appearance of a serializable property that isn\u0027t.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java--76993:77093","promptId":"#NTJ1G","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":76993,"endPos":77093,"startLine":1855,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":1857,"endLineOffset":5,"length":101}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/TransportVersions.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/TransportVersions.java--13388:13475","promptId":"#39TYV","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/TransportVersions.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/TransportVersions.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":13388,"endPos":13475,"startLine":192,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":192,"endLineOffset":91,"length":88}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java--77099:77172","promptId":"#4XYVB","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":77099,"endPos":77172,"startLine":1859,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":1861,"endLineOffset":5,"length":74}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java--10222:10260","promptId":"#7P34R","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/builder/SearchSourceBuilder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":10222,"endPos":10260,"startLine":217,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":217,"endLineOffset":42,"length":39}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/internal/ShardSearchRequest.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/internal/ShardSearchRequest.java--9806:9868","promptId":"#5VZQC","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/internal/ShardSearchRequest.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/internal/ShardSearchRequest.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":9806,"endPos":9868,"startLine":254,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":254,"endLineOffset":70,"length":63}]}]},{"comment":"`skipInnerHits(true)` is set both in `CompoundRetrieverBuilder.createSearchSourceBuilder` (unconditionally) and again in each child\u0027s `extractToSearchSourceBuilder` (guarded by `compoundUsed`). Since `createSearchSourceBuilder` always calls the child with `compoundUsed\u003dtrue`, the child\u0027s assignment is always redundant. Pick one owner of this flag to avoid confusion about which layer is responsible for setting it. If the children\u0027s `extractToSearchSourceBuilder` is the canonical setter (because it\u0027s a public API that could be called from other contexts), then the unconditional set in `createSearchSourceBuilder` is the one to remove.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/KnnRetrieverBuilder.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/KnnRetrieverBuilder.java--10168:10250","promptId":"#7VK1J","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/KnnRetrieverBuilder.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/KnnRetrieverBuilder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":10168,"endPos":10250,"startLine":243,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":245,"endLineOffset":9,"length":83}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/CompoundRetrieverBuilder.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/CompoundRetrieverBuilder.java--11497:11531","promptId":"#0SCF9","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/CompoundRetrieverBuilder.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/CompoundRetrieverBuilder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":11497,"endPos":11531,"startLine":257,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":257,"endLineOffset":42,"length":35}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/RankDocsRetrieverBuilder.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/RankDocsRetrieverBuilder.java--5771:5853","promptId":"#1S2DF","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/RankDocsRetrieverBuilder.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/RankDocsRetrieverBuilder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5771,"endPos":5853,"startLine":144,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":146,"endLineOffset":9,"length":83}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/StandardRetrieverBuilder.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/StandardRetrieverBuilder.java--8298:8380","promptId":"#1BVR7","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/StandardRetrieverBuilder.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/StandardRetrieverBuilder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":8298,"endPos":8380,"startLine":204,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":206,"endLineOffset":9,"length":83}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":257,"line":257,"comment_lines":["[][257]"],"review_comment":["Should we rely on the fact that the compound retriever will always set this? I mean why do we need to set this on the knn and standard retriever too? \r\nWe should also ensure that implementations of the `CompoundRetrieverBuilder` calls `super.createSourceBuilder` first if they want to modify the source builder. `TextSimilarityRankRetrieverBuilder` does it own thing and already diverged (missing the shard id sort and now this new skip inner hits).","That\u0027s a fair point! Will update to ensure that the parent `createSourceBuilder` will always be called, and remove the checks from the individual retrievers. ","Updated."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/CompoundRetrieverBuilder.java","id":36191,"created_at":"2024-11-08T11:38:54Z","original_position":4,"side":"RIGHT","position":13,"submitted_on_commit":"65ce51272c570b65f6bac36474c978537f9e210e","diff_hunk":"@@ -254,6 +254,7 @@ protected SearchSourceBuilder createSearchSourceBuilder(PointInTimeBuilder pit,\n         }\n         sortBuilders.add(new FieldSortBuilder(FieldSortBuilder.SHARD_DOC_FIELD_NAME));\n         sourceBuilder.sort(sortBuilders);\n+        sourceBuilder.skipInnerHits(true);","submitted_line":257},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"`skipInnerHits(true)` is set both in `CompoundRetrieverBuilder.createSearchSourceBuilder` (unconditionally) and again in each child\u0027s `extractToSearchSourceBuilder` (guarded by `compoundUsed`). Since `createSearchSourceBuilder` always calls the child with `compoundUsed\u003dtrue`, the child\u0027s assignment is always redundant. Pick one owner of this flag to avoid confusion about which layer is responsible for setting it. If the children\u0027s `extractToSearchSourceBuilder` is the canonical setter (because it\u0027s a public API that could be called from other contexts), then the unconditional set in `createSearchSourceBuilder` is the one to remove.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/KnnRetrieverBuilder.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/KnnRetrieverBuilder.java--10168:10250","promptId":"#7VK1J","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/KnnRetrieverBuilder.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/retriever/KnnRetrieverBuilder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":10168,"endPos":10250,"startLine":243,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":245,"endLineOffset":9,"length":83}]},{"id":"server/src/main/j